---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Primer | ctfpawned"
  description="Browser devtools and frame-context primer for ctfpawned."
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="hero">
      <h1>Primer</h1>
      <p>
        The targets are sandboxed frames. Use devtools against the frame you are
        testing, and keep the parent shell separate from the vulnerable toy app.
      </p>
    </div>
    <article class="content-panel">
      <h2>Devtools baseline</h2>
      <p>
        Inspect elements, storage, cookies, network activity, and console output
        inside the target frame. If a console command touches the wrong page,
        switch the execution context to the frame whose title matches the
        challenge.
      </p>
      <p>
        Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit expose frame selectors differently, but
        each browser has a console context picker and an element inspector that
        can focus the embedded target.
      </p>
      <h2>Frame context</h2>
      <p>
        The parent page tracks progress and checks flags. The target frame is
        the intentionally vulnerable app. A solution should explain what broke
        in the target and what a production system would change.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
